From f5404ef781bf5277f99026304279171c96f98bd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:47:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/38] libaml: a store into the field Index gives

store() took as its target only references (R, L, A) and names; the
buffer field that Index returns ('u') fell into the default case and
the store was dropped without an error.  So Store (x, Index (BUFF, i))
left the named buffer as it was.  A laptop's ATIF method fills its
reply buffer that way (Lenovo ThinkBook 16 G7 ARP, function 0x10): the
caller got the previous call's reply back.  Such a target is written
through rwfield now, as a field reached through a reference already is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/src/libaml/aml.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/src/libaml/aml.c b/sys/src/libaml/aml.c
index 0c548a383..e12090343 100644
--- a/sys/src/libaml/aml.c
+++ b/sys/src/libaml/aml.c
@@ -845,6 +845,11 @@ store(void *s, void *d)
 	switch(TAG(d)){
 	default:
 		return nil;
+	case 'f':
+	case 'u':
+		/* a field as the target itself: Store (x, Index (BUFF, i)) */
+		rwfield(d, s, 1);
+		return d;
 	case 'A':
 		s = deref(s);
 		/* no break */
